// Storm's Beacon - the pilot episodes. A single-ship STORY universe on the universe_core
// mastlib (Mode: story, no admiral economy). Prof. Storm is VIRTUAL CREW: hail her on the
// Ultra-Beam (with no target selected) for each lead. She reveals the next site; you
// Engage-jump there from the Quests tab and scan the ancient ruin, then hail her again for
// the next heading. Two Storm-gated episodes here; the full campaign (reputation, XORN,
// crafting, Crazy Eddy) builds out from this spine - see STORMS_BEACON.md.

# [Storm's Beacon](storm_s_beacon)
---
Display: Storms Beacon
---
Prof. Storm has a lead on the Beacon - an ancient signal buried in the ruins the old
giants left behind. Hail her for each heading, follow the clues, and stay a jump ahead of
whatever is hunting the same trail.

## [Scenario](scenario)
---
Mode: story
---

## [Lifeforms](lifeforms)

### [Professor Storm](prof_storm)
---
Face: ter #97502d 6 0 6  -2;ter #d7b6a5 0 0;ter #d7b6a5 1 0;ter #d7b6a5 1 2;ter #97502d 8 0 6 -2;ter #fff 12 0 14 -2;ter #fff 1 4;
Roles: advisor, storm
Scene: storm_hail
Color: #6cf
---
Expedition lead and xeno-archaeologist. A host-less advisor - hail her from anywhere on
the Ultra-Beam (no target selected) for the next lead on the Beacon.

#### [Storm is waiting on the Ultra-Beam](storm_ultra_beam)
---
Urge
Every: 4-7m
Title: Ultra-Beam
Whenever: not taught ultra_beam
Until: taught hail_storm
Weight: 10
Escalates: yes
---
% Storm here. When you have a moment - open comms with nothing selected and take Ultra-Beam. That is where I am.
% Professor Storm. I am not on your sensors and I never will be. Clear the comms target, pick Ultra-Beam, and my name is on the list.
%% Captain, I have a heading for you and no way to hand it over. Comms - deselect the target, Ultra-Beam, then me.
%% Storm again. No target selected. That is the whole trick. Ultra-Beam, and we can get on with this.
%%% We are burning daylight out here. Comms - nothing selected, Ultra-Beam, Storm. Please.

### [Crazy Eddy](crazy_eddy)
---
Face: male
Roles: advisor, eddy
Scene: eddy_hail
Color: #fa0
---
A back-channel ship-dealer working the old marches out of a ramshackle hull. Sells gear
nobody else will - some of it even works. A host-less advisor: hail him on the Ultra-Beam
(no target selected) to browse his deals. Cash up front, no refunds.

### [Chief Engineer Vex](chief_vex)
---
Face: female
Roles: advisor, engineer
Scene: vex_hail
Color: #8f8
---
Your chief engineer - keeps this under-gunned little ship flying on scavenged parts and
spite. Hail her on the Ultra-Beam for a read on the ship and a piece of her mind.

#### [Vex mentions the channel](vex_ultra_beam)
---
Urge
Every: 6-9m
Title: Engineering
Whenever: not taught ultra_beam
Weight: 5
---
% Vex, engineering. If you want me, comms with nothing selected, then Ultra-Beam. Beats shouting down a tube.
% Chief Vex here. Same channel as the Professor - no target, Ultra-Beam. I am always on it.

### [Madame Skarr](madame_skarr)
---
Face: female
Roles: advisor, skarr
Scene: skarr_hail
Color: #7c4
---
A Skaraan treasure-broker, hell-bent on selling the Beacon to the highest bidder - and not
much fussed whether it's whole or prised off your wreck. She hired the hunters on your tail.
Hail her on the Ultra-Beam to deal, or to tell her where to go.

### [The Bounty Hunters](bounty_crew)
---
Face: male
Roles: bounty_hunter
Scene: bounty_hail
Color: #db4
---
Two hunters in one battered ship on Madame Skarr's contract. One does the talking; the other,
Dobbs, does the shooting and can't be bothered with the rest. The voice on your comms when the
Second Wind runs you down.

## [Dialogue](dialogue)

### [Professor Storm](storm_hail)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: comms
---
% Storm here, Captain. What do you need?
% Go ahead - I'm knee-deep in old star charts.
% Talk to me. The trail's still warm.

- [Any word on the Beacon?](storm_hail) ; signal storm_check
- [I found something in the ruin](storm_manifest) if carrying clue_manifest >= 1
- [Just checking in](storm_smalltalk)

### [Storm reads the manifest](storm_manifest)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% Read it to me. Read it - no, hold it up, let me - THERE. Do you see that entry? That is not freight. That is a MANIFEST LINE for something they moved out of the station under guard, in the last hour anyone was alive in there.
% You brought me a cargo list. Captain, I could kiss you. Everything else in that station was picked over a century ago; nobody steals paperwork.

Whatever left the Voice's station on that last day, it did not go far - and it did not go
alone. Give me a day with the old charts and I will have you a heading.

- [Take your time.]() ; signal manifest_read
- [What are we looking for?](storm_manifest_more)

### [Storm on what the manifest means](storm_manifest_more)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% Another cache. Not a piece of the Beacon - the giants did not put two of those in one arm of the sky - but the people who scattered them left records, and records are how you find the ones they hid properly.
% A warren, by the description. Somewhere they stopped on the way. Whatever they were carrying, they were carrying it away from something.

- [Understood.]() ; signal manifest_read

### [Professor Storm](storm_smalltalk)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% Watch yourself out there. The Beacon isn't the only thing hunting these ruins.
% Keep the ship quiet and the sensors hot. We find it by being clever, not loud.

// STORM'S EXPEDITION HAILS. A hail is a call the SCRIPT starts - the crew answers it on
// comms - and these are fired declaratively: a quest beat carries `Action: prof_storm hails
// <scene>` and the call goes out the moment that beat goes active. The beats chain off
// reaching a named place inside the ruin, so Storm talks you through the station room by
// room without a line of MAST.
//
// `Presentation: portrait` puts his face on it. Keep each `%` line on ONE line however
// long it runs - a wrapped continuation is an orphan the parser reports against the wrong
// line.

### [Storm on the approach](voice_brief)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Torgoth Megastation
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
Priority: 2
---
% Captain - I have your sensor return and I am looking at it with my mouth open. That is not a wreck. That is a STATION, and it is intact enough to have an inside.
% There it is. Nine kilometres of it. The Torgoth built that when they were giants and they built it to last longer than they did.

The throat on the near face is a docking corridor. They moved freight through it that would
not fit in your hangar bay sideways.

Two things before you go in. The murk in there will cap your engines - that is the station,
not your engineer. And you will not get a jump solution from inside a structure that dense,
so whatever happens in there, you come out the way you went in.

- [Understood. Going in.]()
- [What am I looking for?](voice_brief_what)

### [Storm on what to look for](voice_brief_what)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% The transmitter core. The piece that SPEAKS - the rest of the Beacon is lenses and cradles and cipher work, but this is the part that made noise. It will be at the bottom of the structure, because the Torgoth put the important thing where the station would have to be taken apart to reach it.
% Something that has been trying to transmit for a thousand years. You will know it. Everything else in that station is dead.

- [On my way.]()

### [Storm on the concourse](voice_concourse_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Concourse
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
---
% You are through the throat. Whatever that space opens into, take a moment and LOOK at it before you fly it - I am getting a structural return that says something came down in there.
% Careful. That is a spar across the middle of the concourse, and it did not fall gently.

Three ways on from a Torgoth concourse, as a rule: freight one side, sorting the other,
and the service shaft straight down. The shaft is the one you want. The other two are
where the scavengers will already have been - which does not mean they took everything.

- [Copy.]()

### [Storm on the shaft](voice_shaft_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Service Shaft
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
---
% That shaft runs the depth of the station. Take it slowly - it is a hull's width across and the walls are a thousand years past their last inspection.
% Down. All the way down. Whatever is still alive in there is at the bottom.

Nobody has flown this since the Torgoth did. Mind the walls.

- [Going down.]()

### [Storm on the bay](voice_bay_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Transmitter Bay
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
Priority: 2
---
% That is it. That is the Voice. Captain - that machine has been talking to nobody for ten centuries and it is STILL WARM.
% There. In the cradle. Do you see it? Do you see what they built around it?

Scan it first - I want everything your array can give me before it moves.

Then get a tether on it and carry it out. It will not fit through anything but the way you
came, and it is not going to walk.

- [Understood.]()

### [Storm on the Kralien structure](lens_brief)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Kralien Megastructure
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
Priority: 2
---
% Look at the SHAPE of it, Captain. The Torgoth station was built - beams and bays and right angles. This was bored. Whatever the Kralien used to hollow that out, we do not have it and we never did.
% Same age, same scale, completely different hands. That is what I brought you here to see, and the Lens is only half of why.

The square mouth on the near end is machined - they squared off whatever had to be exact
and let the rest of it curve. Fly in there and follow it round; the structure turns, and
everything past the turn is aimed at one spot.

Same rules as the last one. Your drive will not give you a jump solution inside that, and
the murk will hold you to impulse.

- [Going in.]()
- [Aimed at what?](lens_brief_what)

### [Storm on what it was aimed at](lens_brief_what)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% We do not know. That is the honest answer and it is the reason I have spent eleven years on this. Something at the other end of a very long line.
% The Lens focuses the Voice - takes a shout in every direction and makes it a line. Whatever the giants were talking TO, they wanted it heard in one place and nowhere else.

- [Understood.]()

### [Storm in the gallery](lens_gallery_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Gallery
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
---
% Those walls are smooth. Not polished - SMOOTH, the way a river bed is smooth, and there was never any river in there. Take a reading of that surface for me on your way past.
% Mind the column in the middle of that room. It is holding the ceiling up and it has been doing it a very long time.

Whatever the Kralien left in the side bays, the reclaimers have already been through - but
they were after metal, and they would not have known what glass was worth.

- [Copy.]()

### [Storm at the drum](lens_drum_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Focusing Chamber
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
Priority: 2
---
% There. In the collar - that is the Lens, and it is still ALIGNED, Captain. A thousand years adrift and it is still pointing where they left it pointing.
% A box inside a sphere. Do you see it? They grew the room and then bolted a machined mount into the middle of it, because the mount had to be exact and the room did not.

Scan it before you touch it. I want the alignment recorded - where that thing is looking is
a question I intend to answer eventually.

Then tether it and take it out the way you came.

- [Understood.]()

### [Storm at the bottom of the warren](ash_bottom_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Last Room
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
---
% Nothing. No piece, no array, no machine - and Captain, that is not a wasted trip, that is the FIND. They stopped here. They turned round. Something in that last room told them where to go next and I want it.
% Empty. Good. An empty room somebody dug all the way down to is a room they were using for something they did not want written down anywhere else.

Look for a plate, a slate, anything cut rather than printed. The Kralien did not trust
paper with the things that mattered.

- [Looking.]()

### [Storm on the relay](cipher_brief)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Cipher Relay
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
Priority: 2
---
% I have the chart in front of me and I want you to hear this before you go in: the hole you can see is NOT the way in. It is a room with one exit, and the exit is the way you came. They built a dead end and left it where anyone would find it.
% Read the chart, Captain. The obvious mouth is a decoy. Somebody wanted a search party to find a hole, look inside, and go home.

The real route drops off the floor of that first bubble and doubles back behind it. You
would not guess it and I would not have found it without the warren.

Everything else you know: no jump solution inside, and the murk holds you to impulse.

- [Understood.]()

### [Storm at the dead end](cipher_false_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The False Mouth
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
---
% There it is - nothing. One room, no exits, exactly as the chart says. A thousand years and it still works: anyone without that plate turns round here and calls the relay a myth.
% Empty, and deliberately empty. Look at the floor, Captain. The way on is underneath you and behind you.

- [Taking it slow.]()

### [Storm in the keying chamber](cipher_keying_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Keying Chamber
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
Priority: 2
---
% That is the Cipher. Three of five, Captain - and I am going to say the quiet part out loud: I do not think we are the first people to come looking this century. Something down there has been disturbed.
% There. In the housing. Scan it before you take it, and then take it, and then let us both be somewhere else.

- [Understood.]()

### [Storm on the yard](heart_brief)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Breaker's Yard
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
Priority: 2
---
% That is not a ruin any more, Captain, that is a WORKSITE. Somebody cut a square hole in a thousand-year-old hull and has been carrying it out in pieces, and I am fairly sure I know who.
% Look at the shape of the hole. Nothing that old cuts square like that. XORN has been living in this thing.

Use their cut - it is the only way in and they made it wide enough for a hull, because
they had to get things out through it.

Two more things, and then I will be quiet. Everything else on this trail was empty; this
one is not. And when you have the Heart, do not tidy up. Take it and go.

- [Understood.]()

### [Storm in the yard](heart_yard_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Yard
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
---
% Stacked. Sorted. Labelled, if I am reading that right. This is not looting, Captain, this is a SALVAGE OPERATION - somebody with a schedule and a manifest and every intention of coming back.
% Careful. Anything left on guard in a place like this has been sitting in the dark with nothing to do for a very long time.

- [Copy.]()

### [Storm at the trench](heart_trench_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Service Trench
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
---
% They cut straight down. Whatever the giants put at the bottom of that hull, XORN went through the floor to reach it rather than find the way the builders used.
% It is narrow. I am sorry. There is no other route and you are not going to be able to turn round in there.

- [Going down.]()

### [Storm in the core room](heart_core_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Core Room
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
Priority: 2
---
% There it is. The Heart. And their cutting gear is still sitting around it, Captain, which means they got this far, got a look at what they were cutting, and STOPPED.
% Four of five. Take it - and take whatever paperwork is in that room. I want to know who told them to come here.

Scan it, tether it, and go. If XORN is anywhere on this trail today, it is above you.

- [Understood.]()

### [Storm at the empty cradle](choir_empty_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Empty Cradle
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
Priority: 2
---
% ...it is empty. Captain, I am looking at your feed and the cradle is EMPTY, and it is the wrong size, and I have had you fly four rooms into a building that was never - I was wrong. I want to say that plainly. I was wrong.
% Nothing. Not taken - never there. Look at the cradle: it is cut to a shape somebody GUESSED at.

Give me a moment.

...Right. Two-thirds scale, and copied from the outside, which means somebody saw a working
relay and built a shrine to it. And people who build a shrine write down where the holy
thing went.

There will be a plate. An offering, near the altar - that is what the cradle is to them.
Bring it to me.

- [On it.]()
- [You were wrong.](choir_empty_more)

### [Storm, on being wrong](choir_empty_more)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% I was. Eleven years and I still read what I want to read. Write it down, Captain - the day the professor was wrong - and then help me be right about the next one.
% Yes. And I will be wrong again before this is finished. The trick is to be wrong somewhere cheap, and a room with nothing in it is about as cheap as it gets.

- [Understood.]()

### [Storm on the Sink](sink_scene)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
When: hail
Title: The Sink
Presentation: portrait
Color: #6cf
---
% One room. That is the whole structure - one room and a hole, and everything that has drifted in for a thousand years is still in there, because nothing has ever drifted out.
% No piece here, Captain, and I said as much before you burned the fuel. What is here is traffic: XORN has been in this hulk, and they were careless.

Low, near the wall on the side you came in. Things that settle in a room like that settle
where nobody looks.

- [Copy.]()

// Crazy Eddy's Emporium. The shop is DECLARATIVE dialogue: each deal is a choice gated on
// `if credits >= N`, charged by `; costs N credits`, and wired to a MAST `//signal/eddy_buy_*`
// route (story.mast) that applies the REAL ship modifier. Some deals are honest, some are
// traps, some are a coin-flip - the route decides. The `eddy_sold` line is just his patter;
// the actual up/down result comes back as a comms message from the route.

### [Crazy Eddy](eddy_hail)
---
Speaker: crazy_eddy
When: comms
---
% Eddy's the name, salvage is the game! Step right up, captain.
% You look like a soul in need of an upgrade. Lucky you - I'm having a sale.
% No refunds, no returns, no questions asked. What'll it be?

- [Show me the deals](eddy_shop)
- [Not today, Eddy](eddy_bye)

### [Eddy's Deals](eddy_shop)
---
Speaker: crazy_eddy
---
% Every piece genuine salvage, pried off wrecks with my own two hands. Cash up front!

// Each buy earns `crazy_eddy generous` standing (spending freely makes you his favorite).
// At generous > 15 the "Regulars only" branch unlocks (rep gates a discounted menu) - the
// tactical AND narrative rep use. Rep is per-captain, persisted across episodes.
- [Salvaged Sensor Array - 400cr](eddy_sold) if credits >= 400 ; costs 400 credits, signal eddy_buy_sensor, earns crazy_eddy generous 3
- [Overclocked Impulse Coils - 250cr](eddy_sold) if credits >= 250 ; costs 250 credits, signal eddy_buy_coils, earns crazy_eddy generous 3
- [Reinforced Plating, a STEAL - 150cr](eddy_sold) if credits >= 150 ; costs 150 credits, signal eddy_buy_plating, earns crazy_eddy generous 3
- [Mystery Crate, feeling lucky? - 200cr](eddy_sold) if credits >= 200 ; costs 200 credits, signal eddy_buy_mystery, earns crazy_eddy generous 3
- [That big giant-tech frame - the Resonance Cradle - 500cr](eddy_cradle_sold) if credits >= 500 ; costs 500 credits, signal eddy_buy_cradle, earns crazy_eddy generous 5
- [Regulars only - the good stuff](eddy_loyal) if generous > 15
- [Never mind](eddy_hail)

